<!-- ======================= FORMULAS ======================= -->
<section id="formulas" data-section="formulas" hidden>
  <div class="sheet">
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="eyebrow">Formula sheet</div>
      <h1>Every formula on one page</h1>
      <p class="lede">Read this the night before. t = tax rate, r or k = discount rate, g = growth rate, D = debt, E = equity, V = D + E.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="fs">
    <section><h3>1 · Ratios</h3><dl>
      <dt>Growth</dt><dd>(X<sub>t</sub> − X<sub>t−1</sub>) ÷ X<sub>t−1</sub></dd>
      <dt>CAGR</dt><dd>(End ÷ Start)<sup>1/n</sup> − 1, n = intervals</dd>
      <dt>Margins</dt><dd>Gross profit, EBIT, net income ÷ Sales</dd>
      <dt>ROE / ROBE</dt><dd>NI ÷ ending equity / NI ÷ beginning equity</dd>
      <dt>ROA / pre-tax ROA</dt><dd>NI ÷ total assets / EBIT ÷ total assets</dd>
      <dt>Asset turnover</dt><dd>Sales ÷ total assets</dd>
      <dt>Inventory turnover / days</dt><dd>COGS ÷ inventory / inventory ÷ (COGS/365)</dd>
      <dt>Receivables turnover / collection period</dt><dd>Sales ÷ AR / AR ÷ (Sales/365)</dd>
      <dt>Payables period</dt><dd>AP ÷ (COGS/365)</dd>
      <dt>Current / quick / cash ratio</dt><dd>CA ÷ CL / (cash + securities + AR) ÷ CL / cash ÷ CL</dd>
      <dt>Interval measure</dt><dd>(cash + securities + AR) ÷ daily operating costs</dd>
      <dt>Debt ratio</dt><dd>Interest-bearing debt ÷ (debt + equity)</dd>
      <dt>Equity / assets</dt><dd>1 − liabilities ÷ assets</dd>
      <dt>Times interest earned</dt><dd>EBIT ÷ interest</dd>
      <dt>Common size</dt><dd>Balance sheet ÷ total assets; income statement ÷ sales</dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>2 · Cash cycle &amp; growth</h3><dl>
      <dt>Cash conversion cycle</dt><dd>Days inventory + collection period − payables period</dd>
      <dt>Source of funds</dt><dd>Asset ↓ or liability/equity ↑</dd>
      <dt>Use of funds</dt><dd>Asset ↑ or liability/equity ↓</dd>
      <dt>Retention rate b</dt><dd>1 − payout ratio = (NI − Div) ÷ NI</dd>
      <dt>Internal growth rate</dt><dd>(NI − Div) ÷ beginning assets = b × ROBA</dd>
      <dt>Sustainable growth rate</dt><dd>b × ROBE</dd>
      <dt>DuPont</dt><dd>ROBE = NI/Sales × Sales/Beg. assets × Beg. assets/Beg. equity</dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>3 · Forecasting</h3><dl>
      <dt>External funding need</dt><dd>Proj. assets − (proj. liabilities + equity)</dd>
      <dt>Retained earnings</dt><dd>RE<sub>t−1</sub> + NI − dividends</dd>
      <dt>Net fixed assets</dt><dd>NFA<sub>t−1</sub> + capex − depreciation</dd>
      <dt>Percent of sales</dt><dd>Account<sub>t</sub> = (account ÷ sales)<sub>hist</sub> × Sales<sub>t</sub></dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>4 · Rearranging</h3><dl>
      <dt>Simplified balance sheet</dt><dd>NWC + NFA = Debt + Equity</dd>
      <dt>Net working capital</dt><dd>Cash + AR + inventory − AP − accrued expenses</dd>
      <dt>Real vs financial</dt><dd>AP, accruals = real · bank and long-term debt = financial · taxes = both</dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>5 · Capital structure</h3><dl>
      <dt>Net income</dt><dd>(EBIT − interest) × (1 − t)</dd>
      <dt>Interest tax shield</dt><dd>Interest × t</dd>
      <dt>M&amp;M with taxes</dt><dd>V<sub>L</sub> = V<sub>U</sub> + PV(TS), PV(TS) = t × D (permanent debt)</dd>
      <dt>Expected distress cost</dt><dd>PV(CFD) = probability × PV(costs)</dd>
      <dt>Static tradeoff</dt><dd>V<sub>L</sub> = V<sub>U</sub> + PV(TS) − PV(CFD)</dd>
      <dt>Pecking order</dt><dd>Internal funds → debt → equity</dd>
      <dt>Ex-dividend price</dt><dd>Price before − dividend</dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>6 · Time value &amp; projects</h3><dl>
      <dt>Future value</dt><dd>PV × (1 + r)<sup>t</sup></dd>
      <dt>Present value</dt><dd>FV ÷ (1 + r)<sup>t</sup></dd>
      <dt>NPV</dt><dd>Σ CF<sub>t</sub> ÷ (1 + r)<sup>t</sup> − investment; accept if &gt; 0</dd>
      <dt>IRR</dt><dd>Rate where NPV = 0; accept if &gt; cost of capital</dd>
      <dt>Operating cash flow</dt><dd>NI + depreciation = (Rev − cash costs)(1 − t) + dep × t</dd>
      <dt>Depreciation tax shield</dt><dd>Depreciation × t</dd>
      <dt>Perpetuity</dt><dd>CF ÷ r</dd>
      <dt>Growing perpetuity</dt><dd>CF<sub>1</sub> ÷ (r − g), g &lt; r</dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>7 · Risk &amp; return</h3><dl>
      <dt>Expected cash flow</dt><dd>Σ probability × CF</dd>
      <dt>Discount rate</dt><dd>k = r<sub>f</sub> + risk premium</dd>
      <dt>Portfolio variance</dt><dd>a²σ<sub>A</sub>² + b²σ<sub>B</sub>² + 2ab Cov(A,B)</dd>
      <dt>Correlation</dt><dd>ρ = Cov(A,B) ÷ (σ<sub>A</sub>σ<sub>B</sub>), −1 ≤ ρ ≤ 1</dd>
      <dt>Beta</dt><dd>Cov(r<sub>x</sub>, R<sub>m</sub>) ÷ Var(R<sub>m</sub>); market 1, T-bill 0</dd>
      <dt>CAPM</dt><dd>E(r) = r<sub>f</sub> + β × (R<sub>m</sub> − r<sub>f</sub>), EMRP ≈ 5%</dd>
      <dt>Unlever / relever</dt><dd>β<sub>U</sub> = (E/V) × β<sub>E</sub> · β<sub>E</sub> = β<sub>U</sub> ÷ (E/V)</dd>
      <dt>Pre-tax cost of capital</dt><dd>(D/V)Kd + (E/V)Ke</dd>
      <dt>R<sub>assets</sub></dt><dd>r<sub>f</sub> + β<sub>U</sub> × EMRP</dd>
      <dt>WACC</dt><dd>(D/V) × Kd × (1 − t) + (E/V) × Ke</dd>
    </dl></section>
    <section><h3>8 · Valuing a business</h3><dl>
      <dt>Free cash flow</dt><dd>EBIT(1 − t) + dep − capex − ΔNWC</dd>
      <dt>Terminal value</dt><dd>FCF<sub>T+1</sub> ÷ (k − g)</dd>
      <dt>DCF value</dt><dd>Σ FCF<sub>t</sub> ÷ (1 + k)<sup>t</sup> + TV<sub>T</sub> ÷ (1 + k)<sup>T</sup></dd>
      <dt>NPV of an acquisition</dt><dd>Value of company − price paid</dd>
